#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: Ohio
#> pause: 50
#> must: Kansas
#> must: Ohio
#> must: # command:  sed  -f
#> not: Alabama
#> not: Montana
#> source: t; D
# 23. Only the duplicated lines, like uniq -d. Pement: sed '$!N; s/^\(.*\)\n\1$/\1/; t; D'
# N makes a two-line pattern space. \(.*\)\n\1$ matches when the second line
# repeats the first (\1 is "what the group matched"); s collapses the pair to
# one copy, t jumps to the end so it prints, and otherwise D drops the first
# line and tries again with the next. For plain uniq the sheet has
# sed '$!N; /^\(.*\)\n\1$/!P; D'.
# Try: the uniq form, and watch each state appear exactly once.
$!N; s/^\(.*\)\n\1$/\1/; t; D

#DATA
Alabama
Kansas
Kansas
Montana
Ohio
Ohio
